  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_lockram_cb9e0428fe3282421291de3aacb9a1311ba1817082a41a84f1ab0bc7a218ead3b9">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>lockram, a linen fabric of various qualities for wearing apparel and houshold use (ad. F. locrenan, from Locronan (lit. ‘cell of St. Ronan’), the name of a village in Brittany, where the fabric was formerly made) (OED s.v. lockram) | lockram, a linen fabric of various qualities for wearing apparel and household use (ad. F. locrenan, from Locronan (lit. ‘cell of St. Ronan’), the name of a village in Brittany, where the fabric was formerly made) (OED s.v. lockram) | lockram, a linen fabric of various qualities for wearing apparel and houshold use (ad. F. locrenan, from Locronan (lit. ‘cell of St. Ronan’), the name of a village in Brittany, where the fabric was formerly made) (OED s.v. lockram). Note however p. 168 (pro uno magno balle crest cloth continente 40 pecias lokerames) and p. 203 (pro 2 pakkes lokerams continentibus 81½ pece crest clothe et lokerams) | a linen fabric of various qualities for wearing apparel and household use (ad. F. locrenan, from Locronan (lit. ‘cell of St. Ronan’), the name of a village in Brittany, where the fabric was formerly made) (OED s.v. lockram) | a linen fabric of various qualities for wearing apparel and houshold use (ad. F. locrenan, from Locronan (lit. ‘cell of St. Ronan’), the name of a village in Brittany, where the fabric was formerly made) (OED s.v. lockram) | lockram, a linen fabric of various qualities for wearing apparel and houshold use (ad. F. locrenan, from Locronan (lit. ‘cell of St. Ronan’), the name of a village in Brittany, where the fabric was formerly made) (OED s.v. lockram) 255 (see also dowlas)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
